      "unrated_positions": [],
      "not_audited_positions": [],
      "key_excerpt": "AB 2602 prohibits contractual provisions that would allow for the use of a digital replica of an individual's voice or likeness in place of the individual's actual services, unless the individual gave their consent to a clear, specific description of how the AI would be used. The law requires labor contracts to specify if AI generated replicas of a performer, imitating their likeness or voice, are being used, and mandates that the performer is represented by a union or lawyer in such contracts.",
      "key_excerpt_position": 32
    },
